# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security response headers for the SPA document. TEMPLATED — see below.
#
# WHY THIS IS A SNIPPET AND NOT A `server`-BLOCK BLOCK:
# nginx's `add_header` does NOT merge across configuration levels. A single
# `add_header` inside a `location` block DISCARDS every `add_header` inherited
# from the enclosing `server` block. Both the `/assets/` location and the SPA
# fallback set their own `Cache-Control`, so without an explicit include here
# they would serve the application with NO security headers at all â€” a silent
# failure, since nothing about the response looks wrong.
#
# `always` applies them to error responses too: a 404 or 500 is still a
# document the browser renders.
#
# There is deliberately NO `upgrade-insecure-requests` directive. The stack is
# reachable over plain HTTP on localhost (docker compose publishes :8080), and
# that directive rewrites same-origin subresource requests to https://, which
# would break every asset load locally. HTTPS is enforced by the HSTS header
# below once the app is reached over TLS (ngrok / a real ingress).
#
# There is deliberately no `X-XSS-Protection`. It is deprecated, and current
# browser guidance is to omit it or send `0`; the CSP below is the real control.

# The session token lives in localStorage, so a successful XSS is total account
# takeover. `script-src 'self'` with no 'unsafe-inline' is the control that
# matters most here. Vite emits no inline scripts, so this needs no exception.
#
# `style-src` DOES need 'unsafe-inline': React renders inline `style` props for
# computed geometry (see FlowSpine's stage offsets and the SVG service map), and
# CSP governs presentational style ATTRIBUTES through style-src-attr, which
# falls back to style-src. Removing it means moving those values onto CSS custom
# properties first â€” worth doing, but it is a refactor, not a header change.
# Note this does NOT relax script-src: injected CSS is not a script-execution
# vector, which is why the exception is acceptable here and would not be above.
#
# ★ `form-action` NAMES THE PAYMENT GATEWAY, AND THAT IS THE ONE DELIBERATE
# WIDENING IN THIS HEADER.
#
# The customer completes a card payment on the gateway, and this application
# deliberately stays OUT of the card path: it builds a signed form and the
# browser posts it straight to the gateway, so card details never reach our
# origin. That only works if `form-action` permits the destination — with
# `'self'` alone the form refuses to submit, and the failure is a CSP violation
# in a console rather than anything an operator would connect to a payment
# integration.
#
# It is a named origin and nothing else: no wildcard, no `https:`, no `*`. The
# compromise is bounded to "this form may go to this one host", which is the
# whole of what the checkout needs.
#
# THE VALUE IS A DEPLOYMENT VARIABLE, rendered by envsubst at container start,
# because the gateway host is configuration and a host hardcoded into this file
# would be wrong on every deployment but one — while still LOOKING correct, which
# is the failure mode this repository keeps having to catch.
#
# It is validated by the API at boot (`AMBER_PAY_CHECKOUT_ORIGIN` in
# config/env.ts), so a malformed value fails the deployment loudly instead of
# producing a directive that matches nothing and silently breaks checkout.
add_header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self' ${AMBER_PAY_CHECKOUT_ORIGIN}; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'" always;

add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
add_header X-Frame-Options "DENY" always;
add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
add_header Permissions-Policy "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()" always;

# Only honoured when the response arrives over TLS, so it is inert on localhost
# and effective behind the ngrok tunnel or a real ingress.
add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;